From d116d5cfb46701ee33e7eafa8a9b662dff8546eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 16:08:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: hdmi-codec: fix maybe-uninitialized warning in
 chmap_ctl_get

Initialize 'map' to NULL to silence the gcc -Wmaybe-uninitialized
warning in hdmi_codec_chmap_ctl_get(). The compiler cannot prove
statically that 'map' is always assigned before use inside the loop,
even though the else branch that reads it is only reachable when
chmap_idx != HDMI_CODEC_CHMAP_IDX_UNKNOWN.

Fixes: cd6111b26280 ("ASoC: hdmi-codec: add channel mapping control")
Change-Id: I6756a720b3ea96877782fa95b5ee85067f8d2055
Signed-off-by: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/605878
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c
@@ -382,7 +382,7 @@ static int hdmi_codec_get_ch_alloc_table
 static int hdmi_codec_chmap_ctl_get(struct snd_kcontrol *kcontrol,
 			      struct snd_ctl_elem_value *ucontrol)
 {
-	unsigned const char *map;
+	unsigned const char *map = NULL;
 	unsigned int i;
 	struct snd_pcm_chmap *info = snd_kcontrol_chip(kcontrol);
 	struct hdmi_codec_priv *hcp = info->private_data;
